<section class="section surface" id="roots"><div class="container roots-grid"><div class="roots-media" data-reveal><figure><img <?=responsive_image_attrs(asset('images/journey/field-work.webp'))?> alt="Working in a rural landscape" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><div class="roots-place"><span>Charity · Endarasha</span><strong>Nyeri County, Kenya</strong><small>At the foothills of Mount Kenya</small></div></div><div class="roots-copy" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">Where it begins</span><h2>Nyeri taught me that systems are never abstract for the people living inside them.</h2><p>In Kenya’s central highlands, fertile land, farming, water, roads, markets and family livelihoods are tightly connected. With Mount Kenya shaping the landscape, the relationship between economic progress and stewardship of nature is hard to ignore.</p><p>I grew up in a humble family and learned early what limited means can do to choices and access to opportunity. I also learned that a starting point does not have to become a ceiling. Education, determination, people who open doors and the willingness to act can alter the direction of a life.</p><blockquote>My beginning gave me context, not limits.</blockquote></div></div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><span class="eyebrow">What shapes my lens</span><h2>Three ideas I keep testing against experience.</h2></div><p>They are working principles rather than slogans.</p></div><div class="principle-grid"><article data-reveal><span>01</span><h3>Dignity before labels</h3><p>Where someone begins affects opportunity, but it should never be treated as the final measure of what that person can become.</p></article><article data-reveal><span>02</span><h3>People and nature belong in one equation</h3><p>Livelihoods and prosperity are stronger when the land, water and natural systems that sustain them are treated as assets to steward.</p></article><article data-reveal><span>03</span><h3>Complex change is built together</h3><p>Communities, enterprise, government, capital and knowledge each hold part of the answer. Durable solutions connect them.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="section surface"><div class="container about-focus-grid"><div class="about-focus-intro" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">What I keep exploring</span><h2>Five subjects, connected by the same question: what makes progress useful in real life?</h2><p>These themes guide My Thoughts and much of what I observe through work and travel. Kenya and East Africa are my starting points; comparisons with Europe, the United Kingdom, North America and other places help me test what is local, what is structural and what may travel well between contexts.</p></div><div class="focus-list"><article data-reveal><span>01</span><div><h3>Social entrepreneurship</h3><p>How purpose, enterprise discipline and accountability can create durable social value.</p></div></article><article data-reveal><span>02</span><div><h3>Agribusiness</h3><p>How land, production, finance, infrastructure and markets combine into resilient value chains.</p></div></article><article data-reveal><span>03</span><div><h3>Infrastructure</h3><p>How roads, rail, energy, water, logistics and digital systems expand or constrain opportunity.</p></div></article><article data-reveal><span>04</span><div><h3>Innovation</h3><p>How technology, research, AI and new business models become useful when they solve real problems.</p></div></article><article data-reveal><span>05</span><div><h3>Travel</h3><p>How seeing other places changes what becomes visible in familiar systems back home.</p></div></article></div></div></section>

<section class="section journey-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><span class="eyebrow">Learning by doing and going</span><h2>A life is more than a résumé.</h2></div><p>These moments represent the environments that keep widening my frame of reference.</p></div><div class="journey-grid"><article data-reveal><figure><img <?=responsive_image_attrs(asset('images/journey/early-office.webp'))?> alt="An early office and learning environment" loading="lazy"></figure><span>Learning</span><h3>Curiosity becomes discipline</h3><p>Education widened my questions about institutions, countries and development.</p></article><article data-reveal><figure><img <?=responsive_image_attrs(asset('images/journey/on-the-road.webp'))?> alt="Working and travelling on the road" loading="lazy"></figure><span>Building</span><h3>Ideas meet constraints</h3><p>Work makes questions about people, resources, risk and sustainability unavoidable.</p></article><article data-reveal><figure><img <?=responsive_image_attrs(asset('images/journey/netherlands-windmill.webp'))?> alt="Travelling in the Netherlands" loading="lazy"></figure><span>Perspective</span><h3>Other systems sharpen the eye</h3><p>Seeing how other places organise movement, land and daily life reveals alternatives that are easy to miss at home.</p></article><article data-reveal><figure><img <?=responsive_image_attrs(asset('images/journey/skydiving.webp'))?> alt="A skydiving experience while travelling" loading="lazy"></figure><span>Travel</span><h3>Perspective needs movement</h3><p>New places reveal different ways of organising everyday life and opportunity.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="section surface"><div class="container about-forward"><figure data-reveal><img <?=responsive_image_attrs(asset('images/journey/archery.webp'))?> alt="Practising archery outdoors" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><div data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">What I carry forward</span><h2>Opportunity changed my direction. I want it to travel further.</h2><p>I know what it means to begin with limited choices, and I know how much education, encouragement and a timely opportunity can alter the direction of a life. I do not romanticise either poverty or success.</p><p>The lesson I carry forward is practical: when opportunity reaches you, make something of it — and where possible, widen the path for someone else.</p><div class="personal-note"><strong>Personal views.</strong> The views expressed on this website are my own and do not necessarily represent the views or positions of any business, institution or organisation with which I may be associated.</div><a class="button button-primary" href="<?=url('/my-thoughts')?>">Explore My Thoughts</a></div></div></section>
